/-
This module formalizes the "Singular Series" correction factor for the Hardy-Littlewood k-tuple conjecture.
It defines admissible residues and proves the "q-2" Admissibility Law, which states that for any prime q
and gap g not divisible by q, the number of admissible residues is q - 2.
It also includes corollaries for the Twin Prime case (q=3) and the Brockian Pentagonal case (q=5).
-/

